    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0818" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.5111 European Co-operation/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-15T21:00:00+01:00">July 15, 1932—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—5:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>219. At the convening of the Council this afternoon Sir John Simon made an
                    announcement respecting the recent so-called Franco-British <pb facs="0819"
                        n="699" xml:id="pg699"/> accord.<anchor n="46" xml:id="d489-f1"/> He cited
                    the text of the accord as it has appeared in the press and added certain
                    statements the chief of which were to the following effect: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>There is no relationship between this arrangement and extra European
                            matters;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The Italian and Belgian Governments have signified their
                            adherence;</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>The invitation to other states is not limited to the “inviting states”
                            of Lausanne but is addressed to any European state;</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>The accord does not envisage any organization and is made in the
                            spirit of the Covenant and without prejudice to the League.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>The representative of France<anchor n="47" xml:id="d489-f2"/> associated his
                    Government with the foregoing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
